WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.840
- Mo Brooks was finally served

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.430
in one of the insurrection lawsuits,

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.160
in potentially the most
hilarious way possible.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.711
As you may or may not know, to
serve someone with a lawsuit,

00:00:08.711 --> 00:00:10.827
often you have to physically
hand that to them.

00:00:10.827 --> 00:00:13.260
And often people use process servers.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.470
And in this particular case,

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.070
we have video of when Mo Brooks' wife

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.890
was served with this particular lawsuit.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.880
The process server was trying
to get ahold of Mo Brooks

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:22.713
or his wife.

00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:23.970
She was returning home.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.792
The process server followed
her into the garage,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:29.370
attempted to serve her and
then got back in his car.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.408
At that point, she appears
to be incredibly pissed.

00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:33.200
She gets behind his car,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.871
ostensibly to get his
license plate number,

00:00:34.871 --> 00:00:36.580
possibly to prevent him from leaving,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.340
and then throws a hissy fit.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.080
But that was probably
enough to effectuate service

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.390
in this particular lawsuit.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.880
And yeah, sometimes
that's what you had to do

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.020
to serve someone with a lawsuit,

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.753
so you can see them in court.

